# Line endings.
#
# Deliberately no repo-wide normalization: it would rewrite the working tree for
# every existing clone. Only the paths below are pinned, where content is
# compared byte-for-byte and CRLF breaks it.
#
# Use explicit `text`, not `text=auto`: `auto` does not normalize CRLF on
# checkin here. Scope by extension, not by directory, so a binary asset added to
# these trees is not mangled.

# Read as raw text and asserted verbatim -- agents.test.ts checks that a served
# agent starts with "---\nname: greeter\n", which a CRLF checkout fails.
@quartal/plugin/test/fixtures/**/*.md   text eol=lf
@quartal/plugin/test/fixtures/**/*.ts   text eol=lf
@quartal/plugin/test/fixtures/**/*.json text eol=lf
@quartal/plugin/test/fixtures/**/*.txt  text eol=lf

# Committed build output, vendored from the plugin-docs-web build. The source
# index.html is pinned because it is vite's input: a CRLF input makes vite emit
# CRLF and leave a stray CR at its script-injection point, so a Windows build
# dirties byte-identical content.
@quartal/plugin-docs-web/index.html     text eol=lf
@quartal/plugin/static/**/*.html        text eol=lf
@quartal/plugin/static/**/*.js          text eol=lf
@quartal/plugin/static/**/*.css         text eol=lf
@quartal/plugin/static/**/*.json        text eol=lf
